==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|non|gem-pro|*lītilaz||small, little, few}}. Cognate with {{cog|got|𐌻𐌴𐌹𐍄𐌹𐌻𐍃}}. The comparative and superlative degrees are from {{inh|non|gem-pro|*minnizô}} and {{m|gem-pro|*minnistaz}} respectively, ultimately being degrees of {{der|non|ine-pro|*minu-||small}}, but are already inflections of {{m|gem-pro|*lītilaz}} at the Proto-Germanic stage.

===Adjective===
{{non-adj|minni|minnstr}}

# [[little]], [[small]], [[short]]

====Inflection====
This word has a suppletive inflection, using another root in the [[comparative]] and [[superlative]] forms, than in the [[positive]] form. Before the consonant cluster found in the contracted forms, the central vowel is shortened from ''í'' to ''i'', so that ''lítlir > litlir''. Note also the unexpected ''-nn'' ending in the masculine accusative singular form (''líti'''nn''''' instead of ''litlan''), and the ''-t'' ending in the nominative and accusative singular neuter forms (''líti'''t''''' instead of ''lítilt'').
{{non-decl-adj|lítil|lítil|litl|litl|lítill|asm=lítinn|nsn=lítit|comp=minn|sup=minnst}}

